cff-version: 1.2.0

message: "If you use this companion software, please cite the archived software release and, where appropriate, the corresponding Springer book."

title: "Companion Computational Codes for Computational Metal Additive Manufacturing: Advanced Multiphysics and AI-Enhanced Simulation"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Hosseinzadeh"
    given-names: "Hamed"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8946-1062"

version: "1.0.0"

doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22668105"

repository-code: "https://github.com/Hamedreza7/Computational-Metal-AM-Book"

license: MIT

abstract: >-
  Companion educational source-code implementations for the Springer book
  Computational Metal Additive Manufacturing: Advanced Multiphysics and
  AI-Enhanced Simulation. The repository provides transparent and executable
  implementations of selected computational workflows presented in the book,
  including fusion-based multiphysics modeling, non-fusion metal additive
  manufacturing, neural-network surrogates, Physics-Informed Neural Networks,
  AI-enhanced physics-based modeling, design optimization, reduced-order
  modeling, fatigue assessment, and digital-twin case studies. The examples
  are intended as educational and research starting points that connect
  governing equations and modeling concepts to reproducible computational
  workflows. They are not validated production software for safety-critical
  engineering applications.

keywords:
  - "metal additive manufacturing"
  - "computational modeling"
  - "multiphysics simulation"
  - "laser powder bed fusion"
  - "directed energy deposition"
  - "binder jetting"
  - "physics-informed neural networks"
  - "artificial intelligence"
  - "digital twins"
  - "scientific computing"
